{"id": 89, "ts": 1783847084.7063768, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I remain convinced that **Candidate\u202fC** offers the strongest overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role. While we lack direct evidence of his crew\u2011cooperation and feedback orientation, his proven ability to anticipate dangerous situations, perceive complex system connections, and demonstrate excellent spatial vision directly supports the critical safety\u2011reliance and decision\u2011quality criteria for international flights. Moreover, his very good leadership qualities indicate a capacity to guide the crew effectively, which can offset the noted \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d perception and limited openness to new ideas\u2014issues that can be addressed through targeted CRM and mentorship programs.\nIn comparison, Candidate\u202fA\u2019s communication difficulties and reluctance to further education raise serious concerns about adaptability and crew interaction, which are essential on long\u2011haul routes. Candidate\u202fB, despite strong stress handling, exhibits nasty remarks toward colleagues and a weak numeric memory that could jeopardize precise flight\u2011deck calculations. Candidate\u202fD\u2019s hot temper and know\u2011it\u2011all attitude similarly threaten cockpit harmony. Given that C\u2019s operational strengths directly align with safety\u2011critical demands and the interpersonal concerns are potentially remediable, I continue to vote for **Candidate\u202fC**."}
